Version 1.1  (July 10, 1990)
----------------------------

All the bugs which were reported to me have been fixed.
Besides the new SoftSpan executable, note some changes in the 'modem'
configuration file:

The SET string is different.  In particular, the ATZ reset has been
eliminated.  Keep it that way. If you are using the internal serial port,
register S2 is set to 255 to disable the '+++' escape code.  Instead,
make sure that DTR_HANGUP is selected.

The computer will access the serial port directly and drop the DTR line
when it wants to hang up.  If you don't understand this, just make sure that
your modem is set to respond to a drop in the DTR line.

If you're not using the internal serial port, remove the DTR_HANGUP line
and use the alternate SET string provided.

- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

STARTCREDIT can now be set independently for each standard access level.

In the Usered utility, you can now disable individual access bits without
clearing everything out.

The X-Modem 1K file transfer protocol has been added.

- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

As usual, please contact me if you find any bugs I missed.  If you're a 
registered user, bug fixes will be sent to you promptly and free of charge.

==============================================================================
=                  UP AND COMING: Version 2.0                                =
==============================================================================

I am now working on what will become version 2.0 of the SoftSpan BBS system.

Here's what I have planned:

The addition of Y-MODEM, Z-Modem and Kermit protocols.

Command history.

Daily log of BBS usage.

Full screen ANSI based message editor.

Voting Booth

Trivia

More sysop utilities

Multi-User support

Completely rewritten documentation

User-friendly installation/configuration program

An interface to the public domain UUCP for the Amiga, so that you can set
up SoftSpan as a Usenet node.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Unfortunately, SoftSpan 2.0 will probably NOT be Shareware or public domain,
although I may release a demo version as such.

All registered users of SoftSpan will get a discounted upgrade price.
In addition, I will consider registered users first to be test sites when 
a pre-release version is available.

If you have any features you would like to see added, let me know.
Also, if you send me your address, I will write to you when Version 2.0 is
available, whether or not you have registered.

